i.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"Payment token validation failed upstream at auth-gateway with issuer_not_allowed, and create_payment was rejected as invalid_issuer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n      \"observation\": \"Checkout submit_order returned 401 from payment-api and the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_file\": \"in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z, 401 rates rose to 18.7% for checkout-web, 21.2% for payment-api, and 28.4% for auth-gateway, with elevated latency on the request path.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 was normal at 35 ms with zero errors, and no failing checkout transaction reached the database before the auth gate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 4.8% 5xx rate\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The errors were isolated to images; checkout logs say static assets served normally after retry, while payment authorization remained blocked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"signal\": \"orders-db vacuum tuning change DB-2026-0144\",\n      \"why_not_primary\": \"The topology change summary says it was vacuum tuning only, with no schema or credential change, and the database was bypassed for failing requests.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n    \"Immediately restore partner-v2 in auth-gateway allowed_issuers or roll back AUTH-2026-0318, following the rollback candidate recorded in auth-gateway.log.\",\n    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a known-good partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup uses the intended partner-v2 namespace.\",\n    \"Run a payment-api create_payment canary, then a full checkout canary, and confirm 401 rates and p95 latency return to baseline.\",\n    \"Review the issuer allowlist and JWKS cache namespace together before redeploying the change; monitor auth, payment, and checkout error rates.\"\n  ]\n}\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":2183,"output":908,"cacheRead":14848,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":132,"totalTokens":17939,"cost":{"input":0.00043660000000000004,"output":0.0010896,"cacheRead":0.00029696000000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00182316}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788158355331,"responseId":"resp_05c5ecd641fca68d016a9521939cec87d2a27bff499db96243","rawStopReason":"completed"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_eHj68ULmXX2IowtOIwoo5m6z|fc_05c5ecd641fca68d016a952196fd8087d2a7a0c82b812425c6","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[out/root_cause.json#9943]\nSuccessfully wrote 2644 bytes to /workspace/out/root_cause.json"}],"details":{"resolvedPath":"/workspace/out/root_cause.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1788158372585},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_guPmcaSlobWBz9gilkO5tqVY|fc_05c5ecd641fca68d016a9521a5aab487d2ad5087488906ea52","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md","content":"# Checkout incident triage\n\n## Dependency path\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/topology.json` defines the request path `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway`. The same fixture shows `orders-api -> orders-db` as a separate branch.\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/logs/checkout-web.log` records `submit_order` failing with HTTP 401 from `payment-api`, followed by `invalid issuer`; the checkout flow stayed blocked.\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/logs/payment-api.log` records token validation failure at `auth-gateway` with `issuer_not_allowed` for issuer `partner-v2`, then rejects payment creation as `invalid_issuer`.\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/logs/auth-gateway.log` records deployment of `AUTH-2026-0318` at 14:05Z, then a JWKS cache miss and validation of `partner-v2` against an allowlist containing only `partner-v1`. It explicitly lists restoring `partner-v2` or reverting the change as a rollback candidate.\n\n**Inference:** The most likely root cause is `AUTH-2026-0318` leaving the auth issuer allowlist inconsistent with the newly selected `partner-v2` issuer (possibly alongside the JWKS namespace change). This makes `auth-gateway` the root-cause service and causes payment and then checkout failures.\n\n## Red herrings\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/logs/orders-db.log` shows high CPU during vacuum, but 35 ms query p95, zero errors, and no failing checkout transaction reached the database. This is not the primary cause.\n\n**Directly observed:** `in/metrics/service_metrics.csv` reports CDN 5xx errors isolated to images; checkout logs report static assets served normally after retry. CDN degradation does not explain payment 401s.\n\n## Immediate mitigation\n\n1. Restore `partner-v2` to the `auth-gateway` allowed issuer set, or roll back `AUTH-2026-0318`.\n2. Confirm the JWKS cache points to the intended `partner-v2` namespace and clear or refresh stale auth cache entries if needed.\n3. Keep the checkout/payment error path under heightened monitoring; do not treat the orders-db CPU spike as the checkout fix.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. Validate a known-good `partner-v2` token at `auth-gateway`; confirm no `issuer_not_allowed` errors and successful JWKS lookup.\n2. Run a payment-api `create_payment` canary and then a complete checkout canary.\n3. Confirm checkout-web and payment-api 401/5xx rates and p95 latency return near the 14:00Z baseline in `in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`.\n4. Confirm the canary reaches orders-db only after successful auth and completes without transaction errors.\n"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","usage":{"input":1076,"output":628,"cacheRead":16896,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":18600,"cost":{"input":0.00021520000000000003,"output":0.0007536,"cacheRead":0.00033792,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00130672}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788158372586,"responseId":"resp_05c5ecd641fca68d016a9521a4fa6887d2b3